      "writtenOn": "2023-01-30T04:07:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the slot is reset in onPaused this means you can\u0027t stop a paused keepalive I think. This is racy in any case, but maybe stop would keep working most of the time if you don\u0027t clear the slot in onPause ?\n\nThe ISocketKeepaliveCallback should be used to identify the request in any case, but it feels like using a consistent slot would remove some hard-to-maintain moving parts, and remove the \"tried to resume but no more slots\" case. That might not be too hard too, making KeepaliveTracker.handleStartKeepalive use the slot in KeepaliveInfo instead of searching for one, having the slot in the KeepaliveInfo constructor, and moving findFirstFreeSlot to AutomaticOnOffKeepalive",
      "revId": "7978020d884a4f83b22e8ea3cd561c80b9d3290e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
