      "writtenOn": "2023-02-03T13:45:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "b/267106526 is about having tests to make sure this works.\n\nI do not see any problem with multiple links to death – this is explicitly intended usage, and I strongly think there is no need of principle to only have one link to death so this should really not be a goal. Of course, conversely I have no objection to having only one if that\u0027s simpler ; I think we should have whichever style is simpler to maintain.\n\nInstead the goal should be to make sure this works in all cases and is as maintainable as possible. If the simplest solution is only one link, let\u0027s have one link. If the simplest solution is to have two, let\u0027s have two.\n\nObserve how this code was already broken if the app unregisters and dies in the span of a single handler loop. I don\u0027t think this patch should be held responsible for fixing this existing issue.",
      "parentUuid": "71e89761_dbffecff",
